window.EN={"1":"On the continent of Elibe, humankind, which had no natural predators, spread far and wide","2":"and built up countless civilizations.","3":"To the west, the Kingdom of Etruria, proud of its sophisticated culture and the most prosperous in the land,","4":"and to the east, the Kingdom of Bern, which valued a plain but steady culture and a spirit of simple strength.","5":"These two kingdoms formed the center, with smaller powers strung out between them.","6":"The Lycian League, where multiple lords joined hands against the two great kingdoms,","7":"the knighthoods of the Ilia region, who cleared the wastelands together with the people,","8":"and the tribes of the Sacae region, who rode their horses across the vast plains.","9":"Through the balance of these powers, aside from the occasional small conflict,","10":"the continent as a whole had kept its stability...","11":"But that stability suddenly and fragilely crumbled away.","12":"The great eastern kingdom of Bern, under the order of King Zephiel, began invading one region after another.","13":"The Bernese army invaded regions such as Sacae and Ilia, utterly destroying all who resisted.","14":"And now that hand had begun to reach toward the Lycia region as well.","15":"Roy, the eldest son of Lord Eliwood of Pherae, who governed the territory around Pherae in eastern Lycia,","16":"had gone to study in Ostia, the greatest city in Lycia, in order to become the next lord.","17":"But his father Eliwood, who was ill, suddenly ordered him to return home.","18":"That was after, as Hector's representative,","19":"Lilina, the beloved daughter of Eliwood's close friend Lord Hector of Ostia, had set out for Pherae to visit him.","20":"Chasing right after her, Roy, along with Pherae's loyal retainers who followed him,","21":"brought along Bors, the Ostian great knight assigned to escort Lilina on her way back,","22":"and set out by sea for his homeland of Pherae.","23":"And so our story begins just as Roy and his companions return to the edge of Pherae's domain...","24":"Boss!","25":"Looks like they've shut themselves up in the castle.","26":"Heh. Even Lord Eliwood of Pherae, once hailed as the finest knight in Lycia—","27":"—I guess even he can't beat an illness, huh?","28":"Heheh, with Bern attacking, this area's left pretty thin on defenses.","29":"Your read on it was spot on, boss!","30":"Course it was. But there's no telling when help might show up.","31":"Alright, you lot! Finish off everyone in that castle before that happens!","32":"Do that, and all the treasure in the castle's ours for the taking.","33":"Heh heh heh, the castle's not the only place with treasure, you know.","34":"While they're all busy over there, how about we hit the village too?","35":"Lord Eliwood, this is terrible!","36":"Bandits from Mount Bolm are right outside...","37":"I see...","38":"Ngh... if I weren't in this condition, I'd never let them have their way... *cough* *cough*","39":"Uncle...","40":"Lilina, go and hide. This place will soon become a battlefield.","41":"No... I'll fight too! I'll fight as well!","42":"Don't talk nonsense.","43":"If anything were to happen to you, I wouldn't be able to face Hector again.","44":"Face Father? B-but...","45":"It'll be fine. Roy should be back nearby by now.","46":"If we can just hold out until then, we should manage somehow.","47":"Marinus!","48":"Send a messenger to Roy and the others — tell them it's urgent!","49":"Y-y-yes, sir!","50":"Isn't that Lance? What's wrong? You look frantic.","51":"Lord Roy! Bandits have surrounded the castle and are attacking it!!","52":"Wh-what!? What's happened to Lord Eliwood and the others?","53":"Right now he's drawing the enemy into the castle to hold them off, but in his condition...","54":"L-Lord Lance, was it!? What about Lady Lilina? Is she safe?","55":"! You must be from Ostia. Lady Lilina is in the castle too.","56":"As long as she stays by Lord Eliwood's side, there's no need to worry, but...","57":"—that won't last forever.","58":"Damn it... if I'd known this would happen, I never should have let Lilina go on ahead.","59":"Lord Roy, there's time to regret this later. For now, to the castle!","60":"Wolt is right. Lord Roy, let's hurry!","61":"Right.","62":"Alright, let's go, everyone! We're going to rescue Father and the others!","63":"Tch! They're already here?","64":"But I'm not about to let you get to that castle so easily!!","65":"You should take good care of your money, you know? Life is long, and you never know what might happen.","66":"If you waste it, you might end up suffering for it later.","67":"If you want to win a battle, you'd do well to make good use of the terrain.","68":"If you're in a forest, the trees get in the way, so enemy attacks should be less likely to hit you.","69":"They say Bernese soldiers have crossed the border and invaded Lycia.","70":"The lords are forming an alliance to meet them in battle, but the enemy is that great nation Bern, after all.","71":"And Lord Eliwood, who we're counting on, is in that condition... It's worrying, isn't it...","72":"Um! You're heading to the castle now, aren't you?","73":"Here, it's not much, but it's a token of feeling from everyone in the village.","74":"Please put it to good use!","75":"You fools.","76":"Giving us this much trouble, and from the likes of them!","77":"Gah...? Strong...","78":"Father! Lilina!","79":"Oh, Roy!","80":"Roy!","81":"Father! Lilina!! ...I'm glad you're both safe.","82":"Roy, you've come a long way. Well done.","83":"No, more importantly, Father, how is your health?","84":"I'm fine. As you can see, I'm still alive and well enough.","85":"Now then, Roy, let's get right to it.","86":"You understand why I went to the trouble of calling you back to Pherae... don't you?","87":"It's so that I can lead Pherae's army in your place and join the Lycian Alliance army, isn't it?","88":"Indeed. As you know, the great eastern nation of Bern has begun its invasion of this land of Lycia.","89":"We must send out an army to defend this land, in accordance with the ancient pact of the lords' alliance.","90":"Yes, sir.","91":"I was reluctant to call you back while you were still partway through your studies abroad, but...","92":"After all, with this body of mine... I can't very well be the one holding everyone back.","93":"Father...","94":"Uncle Eliwood, I'll go together with Roy!","95":"Father should be with the main force of the Alliance army, and if my magic can be of even a little help to Roy...","96":"No, Lilina. You should go back to Ostia.","97":"Eh... why?","98":"In Ostia, with no lord there right now, the people must be living in anxious uncertainty every day.","99":"As the heir of Ostia, you have a duty you must fulfill.","100":"You understand, don't you?","101":"...Yes.","102":"Roy, first go and join up with the mercenary company already arranged at the border with Bern.","103":"I'll have Marinus go with you as well. He's timid, but he's knowledgeable, so he'll be useful.","104":"Thank you for everything, Father.","105":"It'll be fine. I know you can do it.","106":"Go and fight splendidly, as one who will inherit the House of Pherae!","107":"Yes, sir!","108":"Bors... I have a favor to ask.","109":"I understand already.","110":"In Lady Lilina's place, I shall accompany him — I will surely protect Lord Roy.","111":"Thank you.","112":"Roy... take care, okay?","113":"Right. You too, Lilina!"};
